From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:17:19 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: drop the stale fifth-GPHY warnings

Two comments in this board file still warn that the fifth GPHY's
firmware entry is missing and that the board therefore has no ethernet
at all: the file header, and the ordering note on the WAN port. Both
stopped being true when the fifth entry was added, and &gphy_fw has
carried all five since.

The header now says what is actually the case -- the WAN PHY answers
MDIO and its port instantiates alongside the four LAN ones -- and what
is genuinely still owed, which is traffic rather than description. Link
coming up is not the same claim as forwarding, and the port-to-port
traffic matrix has not been exercised yet.

The ordering note keeps the part of itself that is worth keeping. The
dependency it describes is real and merely satisfied: remove an entry
from that list and the WAN PHY stops answering MDIO, no phy_device is
created, phylink_of_phy_connect returns -ENODEV, and because probe
requires every declared port to come up, that one failure takes the four
working LAN netdevs with it. Worth knowing before trimming the list;
just not worth phrasing as something outstanding. It also pointed at
&gphy_fw as being below it, which it is not.

Comments only. The built DTB is byte-for-byte identical.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
index 5ac493ec88c0..810e9b6462a3 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
@@ -284,14 +284,10 @@ gphy_wan: ethernet-phy@1 {
  * scheduler block 12, DMA1TX channel 15. Note the controller: every LAN port
  * egresses via DMA2TX, this one does not.
  *
- * ⚠ ORDERING: this port cannot come up until the fifth GPHY is added to
- * &gphy_fw below. Without its firmware the WAN PHY does not answer MDIO, no
- * phy_device is created for gphy_wan, and phylink_of_phy_connect returns
- * -ENODEV -- which is NOT deferred and NOT confined to this port. Probe
- * requires every declared port to come up, so the failure rolls back the four
- * working LAN netdevs with it and the board ends up with no ethernet at all.
- * Adding the fifth GPHY is three appended entries; see the comment on
- * &gphy_fw.
+ * This port depends on the fifth GPHY's firmware entry, which &gphy_fw above
+ * carries along with the other four. Probe requires every declared port to
+ * come up, so that one failure would roll the four working LAN netdevs back
+ * with it and leave the board with no ethernet at all.
  */
 &intel_xrx500_net {
 	port@4 {
